rd, light colored—yes sheep. Goats typically have straight hair, often beards, different face. These faces look like sheep faces (the one in center facing away shows a woolly rump, the right one shows a sheep head with woolly face). Yes sheep.\n\nSo I'll correct: The animals are sheep, not goats.\n\nI'll provide a concise answer. The user likely expects a single word in the blank. I'll say \"sheep\".\n\nLet me write reasoning in English (user's language).\n</think>\n\nSheep\n\nThe animals grazing in the field are **sheep**, not goats. You can tell by their thick, rounded woolly fleece (goats have short hair), their stocky body shape, and the way they're feeding together in a flock on open pasture. So the correct word for the blank is **sheep**.<|im_end|>",
